  "id": "e8d3af04-932e-59a3-8edb-24d35e3efe65",
  "slug": "swicy-gyro-dogs-recipe-12005925",
  "name": "Swicy Gyro Dogs",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "In these swicy gyro dogs, we give America's favorite tube-shaped meat a Mediterranean makeover. And, because \"sweet and spicy\" is just too much to say, the new word of the day is \"swicy.\" Grilled over charcoal, and dressed gyro-style, the texture lands between burger and hot dog, and the flavor is simply spectacular.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "For gyro dogs, add lamb and beef to a large bowl; add onion, garlic, breadcrumbs, rosemary, oregano, salt, black pepper, cumin, paprika, cayenne, cinnamon, and cold water. Mix very thoroughly with clean hands until all the ingredients are emulsified together and the meat starts to feel sticky, about 2 minutes. For a firmer, \u201csnappier\u201d texture, this step can be done in a food processor."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Divide mixture into 8 equal portions using a digital scale. Place each portion on a piece of plastic wrap and using damp fingers, form into a 7-inch long log. Roll each portion up in the plastic, pressing and smoothing as you do to form the hot dog shape. Finish by twisting the ends of the plastic wrap together."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Refrigerate for a minimum of 4 hours, but preferably overnight."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "For glaze, stir honey, lemon juice, Sriracha, and cayenne together in a small bowl; set aside until needed."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "For garlic sauce, stir Greek yogurt, garlic, lemon juice, salt, and olive oil together; thin sauce as needed with water, and refrigerate until needed."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Prepare a charcoal grill or gas grill for medium-high heat."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Grill hot dogs for about 8 minutes, turning every 2 minutes, or until the meat feels firm and springs back to the touch. Brush glaze over the dogs, and turn over. Brush the other side, and turn again. Repeat the glazing, letting each side cook for about 30 seconds between brushings, until the glaze is gone, and meat is cooked through."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "To serve, sauce the insides of the buns before placing the hot gyro dogs in. Place sliced tomatoes between the bun and the gyro dog, and top with more garlic sauce. Finish with red onions and cucumbers."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 30,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 20,
